7] [17592186478319 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478319 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478319 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478319 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8e540d7b-743f-5bd7-a258-f559a1a1adde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478321 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478321 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478321 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478321 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478321 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "905a5d8b-fc52-5fb2-af2a-3605fabca6ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478325 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478325 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478325 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478325 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478325 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a3934810-291e-50dd-a02f-1abe03f05b32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478327 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186477769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478327 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478327 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478327 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186477769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478327 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b18b7f1a-9848-5ccf-aabe-0086594b08a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1089 #edb/ref 17592186478370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478369 #edb/ref 1090 #uuid "ee683fb6-8dcb-5c70-bc16-77d5deb6c97d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186478468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186478474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186478477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186478489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186478492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186478496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186478497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1085 "A foundation is organizing a juice and cake sale for charity." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1086 #uuid "bda8c7b2-ecbe-5320-9b0d-e5ab48e508b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478370 #edb/ref 1087 #edb/ref 17592186478492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478378 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478378 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134041" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478378 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478378 #edb/ref 1071 "Mark drank $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the amount of orange juice that he bought. What **exact** amount of juice did Mark drink?\n\n*Remember that Mark bought $\\frac{7}{4}$ liters of orange juice.*\n\nMark drank\n{{field-1}}\nliters of orange juice." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478378 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "17030b91-3cba-5c59-ac6a-c1eb417052bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478378 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that Mark has $\\frac{7}{4}$ of a liter of orange juice.\n\nTo find the fraction of a liter that Mark drank, we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{2}$ by $\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 7}{2\\times 4}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mike drank $\\frac{7}{8}$ liters of orange juice." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478390 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478390 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478390 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478390 #edb/ref 1071 "Margaret and Ivana each bought $3$ blackberry muffins and $5$ strawberry muffins. In total, they bought$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$muffins." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478390 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "372b47e2-6ed6-5dd6-9cf6-680592eef643" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478390 #edb/ref 1074 "We must write and evaluate an expression representing the total number of muffins.\n\nSince each of them bought $3$ blackberry muffins and $5$ strawberry muffins, the number of muffins each of them bought is:\n\n$$\n{{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{blackberry muffins}}+{{5}_{⏟}}_{\\text{strawberry muffins}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person bought this number of muffins, and there are $2$ people, we must multiply the number of muffins by $2.$ Therefore, the total number of muffins is:\n\n$$\n{{(3+5)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{2}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+5)\\times 2 & =(3+5)\\times 2 \\\\  & =8\\times 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n8\\times 2=16\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478402 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478402 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134039" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478402 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478402 #edb/ref 1071 "Of the $3$ liters of strawberry juice Mark bought, he gave $\\frac{2}{5}$ liters to his niece Rose. As a mixed number, Mark has$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters of strawberry juice left." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478402 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "568d8931-746a-5ddb-bec0-b2b44679e4f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478402 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out how much strawberry juice Mark has left, we must calculate the difference $3-\\frac{2}{5}.$\n\nTo subtract $\\frac{2}{5}$ from $3,$ we need to express the whole number $3$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $5.$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nThen, we put this fraction over a denominator of $5$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{15}{5}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{15-2}{5}=\\frac{13}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n13÷5=2\\,\\text{R}\\,3=2\\,\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mark has $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ liters of strawberry juice left." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478432 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478432 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134037" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478432 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478432 #edb/ref 1071 "If $8$ people made all the muffins for the sale, and each made the same number of muffins, then each person made{{field-1}}\nmuffins." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478432 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad2f9bd5-68e3-5ec1-9893-522d4b4c3aca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478432 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that there are $336$ muffins in total. So, each person made $336÷8$ muffins.\n\nWe start by writing down the question using long division notation:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}3\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNotice that $3$ (the number of hundreds in $336$) is less than the divisor $8.$ Therefore, we should consider both the hundreds and tens:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}3\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$↓$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $33÷8=4\\,\\text{R}\\,1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over tens: $4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $8\\times 4=32$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $33-32=1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Bring down: $6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNext, we consider the ones:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}3\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\boxed{\\text{0}}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $16÷8=2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over ones: $2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $8\\times 2=16$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $16-16=0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe get the remainder $0$, so the division is done.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n336÷8=42.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478443 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134036" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478443 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478443 #edb/ref 1071 "At the sale, there are $14$ tables. If there are $24$ muffins on each table, then there are{{field-1}}\nmuffins in total." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478443 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bdb9c372-6491-56bd-a5e0-6ea4e60521c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478443 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the total number of muffins, we need to multiply $14$ by $24.$\n\nSo, we write it this way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  &  &  & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the ones:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}14\\times 4=56\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the tens:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}14\\times 20=280\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}56+280=336\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $14\\times 24=336.$\n\nTherefore, there are $336$ muffins in total." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134040" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478459 #edb/ref 1071 "After Rose takes her share of strawberry juice, Mark's remaining amount of strawberry juice is{{field-1}}\nthan the remaining amount of orange juice because $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$\n{{field-2}} $\\frac{7}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "edc909fc-f87e-5b26-96f1-797620d48727" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478459 #edb/ref 1074 "Mark has $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ liters of strawberry juice and $\\frac{7}{4}$ liters of orange juice remaining.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $5\\times 4=20.$\n\nTo put $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{13}{5}=\\frac{13\\times 4}{5\\times 4}=\\frac{52}{20}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{7}{4}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{7\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{52}{20}$ and $\\frac{35}{20}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $52>35,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{52}{20}>\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n> \"After Rose takes her part of strawberry juice, Mark's remaining amount of strawberry juice is $>$ than the remaining amount of orange juice because $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}>\\frac{7}{4}.$\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478467 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478467 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134038" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478467 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478467 #edb/ref 1071 "Mark bought $3$ liters of strawberry juice and $\\frac{7}{4}$ liters of orange juice. How much juice did Mark buy in total? Express your final answer as a mixed number.\n\nMark bought$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters of juice." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478467 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ff575d67-9751-56f2-8a79-bde7f1b08899" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478467 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out how much juice Mark bought in total, we have to calculate the following sum:\n\n$$\n3+\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nTo add $3$ and $\\frac{7}{4},$ we need to express the whole number $3$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $4.$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nThen we put this fraction over a denominator of $4$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 4}{1\\times 4}=\\frac{12}{4}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{4}+\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nTo add two fractions with like denominators, we add the numerators and keep the denominators the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{4}+\\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{12+7}{4}=\\frac{19}{4}\n$$\n\nExpressing our answer as a mixed number, we have\n\n$$\n19÷4=4\\,\\text{R}\\,3=4\\,\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mark bought $4\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ liters of juice in total." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478468 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0051cc2c-ee6b-55c4-85b8-6e661e80048f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478468 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186478378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478473 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "21df9c39-a6df-56ad-910b-a7258b5d0294" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478473 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186478369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478474 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186478496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478474 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22427de6-b7ba-559f-99d1-f96d0422df3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478474 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186478443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478477 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186478497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478477 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "57044afd-796c-59ea-8ea1-dade866e8487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478477 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186478467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478489 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186478468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478489 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bde6e6a7-412b-5641-a01b-e34029b71739" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478489 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186478459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478492 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186478474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478492 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d1965ca0-0b81-52c0-8709-ba62075b6107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478492 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186478390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478496 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186478477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478496 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "efb71f32-1643-58ca-b666-f2e38c76e03e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478496 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186478432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478497 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186478489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478497 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fab18979-877e-5675-b488-2c0be5962d5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478497 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186478402 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
